  "question": {
    "text": "Let $(x, y)$ be any point on the parabola $y^2=4 x$. Let $P$ be the point that divides the line segment from $(0,0)$ to $(x, y)$ in the ratio $1: 3$. Then, the locus of $P$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2pWUb",
      "text": "\n$x^2=y$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "IF0GC",
      "text": "\n$y^2=2 x$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "No7ne",
      "text": "\n$y^2=x$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "f3Yr6",
      "text": "\n$x^2=2 y$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\text { By section formula, }\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/NZeJW46lYjK_Tb4Ljhd5REr04ncqMpNoSecFzLx2gXo.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$h=\\frac{x+0}{4}, k=\\frac{y+0}{4}$\n$\\therefore \\quad x=4 h$ and $y=4 k$\nSubstituting in $y^2=4 x$,\n$(4 k)^2=4(4 h) \\Rightarrow k^2=h$\nor $y^2=x$ is required locus.",
